    ["邦尼开酒吧，做人口买卖，身边永远围着漂亮女人，讨厌一切男人。没人关心她脖子上护符的来历，大家都认为她坏到骨子里。\n红宝石护符来自她曾经的舞蹈搭档，那个和她一起从街头跳舞跳进贝克兰德的男人。他们约好要一起站在最亮的聚光灯下，但名利场是一把裹着绸缎的刀。她在其中沉浮，与搭档渐行渐远。终于有一天，那人的刀尖刺向了她。\n有人问邦尼，你不恨吗，她说恨。\n那为什么还戴着护符？\n邦尼把护符塞进领口：“我这辈子，就信过那一个人。后来我亲手枪毙了他。”\n宝石还在，疤痕还在，恨也还在，像一片烧不完的余烬。"] = "Bonnie runs a bar, traffics people, is always surrounded by beautiful women, and hates all men. No one cares about the origin of the amulet on her neck; everyone thinks she is rotten to the core. \n The ruby amulet came from her former dance partner, the man who danced with her from the streets into Backlund. They promised to stand under the brightest spotlight together, but the vanity fair is a knife wrapped in silk. She drifted within it, growing distant from her partner. Finally, one day, that man's blade turned toward her. \n Someone asked Bonnie if she hated him, and she said she did. \n Then why still wear the amulet? \n Bonnie tucked the amulet into her neckline: \"In this life, I only trusted that one person. Later, I shot him dead with my own hands.\" \n The gem remains, the scars remain, and the hatred remains, like a pile of embers that can never be burned out.",
